1
00:00:00,251 --> 00:00:01,836
Aren't you earning enough?

2
00:00:01,919 --> 00:00:03,546
Do really need money that badly?

3
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:05,256
I'll use it to pay off our debts.

4
00:00:05,339 --> 00:00:06,465
Once that's done,

5
00:00:06,549 --> 00:00:08,884
I can finally do what I've always wanted.

6
00:00:08,968 --> 00:00:10,803
You know, I know a producer

7
00:00:10,886 --> 00:00:13,013
who's planning to produce an indie film.

8
00:00:13,097 --> 00:00:14,807
I think you're fit for the lead role.

9
00:00:18,144 --> 00:00:18,978
No! Wait!

10
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,021
-Wait, just a second.
-Patricia!

11
00:00:21,105 --> 00:00:23,524
Hey! What are you doing to my daughter?

12
00:00:27,069 --> 00:00:29,405
Do you think I don't tell myself that?

13
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:32,283
I'm stupid! I'm so stupid!
I'm such an idiot!

14
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:40,750
Hey.

15
00:00:41,834 --> 00:00:44,211
-Are you okay?
-Oh.

16
00:00:44,754 --> 00:00:48,466
Yes. It's nothing. Just a sprain.

17
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:50,092
That was intense.

18
00:00:50,676 --> 00:00:52,428
You were like an action star back there.

19
00:00:53,012 --> 00:00:53,971
That's what all that coffee does to you.

20
00:00:59,435 --> 00:01:01,604
You needed help, Patricia.

21
00:01:03,189 --> 00:01:04,440
Thanks.

22
00:01:04,815 --> 00:01:06,192
Are you okay?

23
00:01:07,526 --> 00:01:09,361
You're still joking around.

24
00:01:09,445 --> 00:01:10,780
Yes.

25
00:01:11,781 --> 00:01:13,574
I'm over it now.

26
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:15,493
Besides, I talked to the police.

27
00:01:15,576 --> 00:01:18,245
They're taking them to the station.

28
00:01:18,496 --> 00:01:20,331
I'm not asking what happened.

29
00:01:30,216 --> 00:01:33,093
I'm asking how you're feeling.

30
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:35,888
Alive and kicking.

31
00:01:59,495 --> 00:02:03,290
You don't have to pretend you're strong
all the time, Patricia.

32
00:02:03,374 --> 00:02:04,750
It's okay.

33
00:02:06,210 --> 00:02:08,170
It's okay to let it all out.

34
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:44,582
I can handle it.

35
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,918
I'll get through this.

36
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:51,964
There's nothing I can't handle.

37
00:03:05,311 --> 00:03:06,312
Mm.

38
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:19,867
I'm right here, okay?

39
00:03:23,245 --> 00:03:24,288
Anytime.

40
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:27,541
And don't worry.

41
00:03:28,334 --> 00:03:31,253
I won't tell anyone
at the office you cried.

42
00:03:43,599 --> 00:03:44,725
Don't worry.

43
00:03:46,644 --> 00:03:47,937
I'll get through this.

44
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:50,731
I'm not planning to stay down for long.

45
00:03:51,815 --> 00:03:55,361
If I let everything
that's happened in my life get to me…

46
00:03:56,487 --> 00:03:58,489
you might not be able
to talk to me anymore.

47
00:05:20,195 --> 00:05:21,613
Oh, hello, Sis!

48
00:05:25,909 --> 00:05:27,036
Sis?

49
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:30,456
Are you okay? You look pale.

50
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:33,292
Oh, dear.

51
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,919
I'm glad you're home.

52
00:05:40,424 --> 00:05:41,675
Did something happen?

53
00:05:41,967 --> 00:05:43,469
I'm just tired, Dad.

54
00:05:43,927 --> 00:05:44,928
Are you sure?

55
00:05:48,599 --> 00:05:50,976
The nerve of those people!

56
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:53,062
Why, Mom? What happened?

57
00:05:53,437 --> 00:05:55,773
I got fired from the municipal office.

58
00:05:55,856 --> 00:05:56,899
What?

59
00:05:57,524 --> 00:06:00,986
They accused me of taking bribes.

60
00:06:01,445 --> 00:06:03,655
That's not right.

61
00:06:03,989 --> 00:06:05,115
Let's file a complaint.

62
00:06:05,657 --> 00:06:06,658
But, Mom…

63
00:06:07,409 --> 00:06:08,869
Were you really taking bribes?

64
00:06:08,952 --> 00:06:11,246
April, watch your mouth.

65
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,915
That's not the point.

66
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:15,292
The point is, I just got fired.

67
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:19,129
What do we do now?

68
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:22,216
Patricia, get me some water.

69
00:06:23,425 --> 00:06:24,510
Yes, Mom.

70
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:36,688
Dear…

71
00:06:37,314 --> 00:06:39,399
What are we going to do now?

72
00:06:40,317 --> 00:06:41,443
Uh…

73
00:06:43,278 --> 00:06:44,446
It'll be okay.

74
00:06:44,947 --> 00:06:46,573
I have a job, remember?

75
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:50,410
-I'll just go change.
-Patricia.

76
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:52,538
Are you sure you're okay?

77
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:55,874
Yes, Dad.

78
00:06:57,084 --> 00:06:58,627
I just need some rest.

79
00:07:17,646 --> 00:07:20,566
Diana, did you get any sleep?

80
00:07:21,150 --> 00:07:22,776
-You need to rest.
-I'm fine.

81
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:24,194
I'm fine.

82
00:07:24,611 --> 00:07:28,866
I bet you're thinking about what happened
to Patricia again, aren't you?

83
00:07:29,199 --> 00:07:30,951
It can't happen again.

84
00:07:32,744 --> 00:07:34,204
What's your plan?

85
00:07:34,705 --> 00:07:36,790
She needs to get back on the right path.

86
00:07:36,874 --> 00:07:38,709
She needs to go back to school.

87
00:07:39,418 --> 00:07:41,545
I can't rely on Martin.

88
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:43,380
They're taking advantage of my daughter.

89
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:46,216
There's nothing we can do to stop you.

90
00:07:46,675 --> 00:07:48,218
You are a mother, after all.

91
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:49,970
But, Diana, think about it,

92
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:52,222
Patricia is no longer a kid.

93
00:07:52,306 --> 00:07:54,141
I'm just worried about her.

94
00:07:56,059 --> 00:07:59,771
All you do is think about everyone, Diana.

95
00:07:59,855 --> 00:08:02,316
It's always about Patricia, the company,

96
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:04,318
the employees, and the clients.

97
00:08:05,027 --> 00:08:07,696
Try putting yourself first sometimes.

98
00:08:08,030 --> 00:08:11,116
Who else should I think about, Nanny Cora?

99
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:13,493
Oh, Diana. You're not getting any younger.

100
00:08:13,577 --> 00:08:15,787
You will be retiring in a few years.

101
00:08:15,871 --> 00:08:17,623
What would your life be like then?

102
00:08:17,706 --> 00:08:20,209
Have you ever thought
of spending your life with someone?

103
00:08:20,292 --> 00:08:22,878
A partner who'll take care of you.

104
00:08:24,296 --> 00:08:26,715
Oh, please, I gave up on that
a long time ago.

105
00:08:27,257 --> 00:08:29,551
I don't think I can trust someone again.

106
00:08:29,635 --> 00:08:32,054
Not all men are like Martin, you know.

107
00:08:32,387 --> 00:08:35,057
Do you know any sensible man? Hmm?

108
00:08:37,059 --> 00:08:40,187
A decent man who's successful, smart,

109
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:42,231
and will not be intimidated by me.

110
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:44,316
Someone sensible, hmm…

111
00:08:44,650 --> 00:08:45,943
and doesn't have vices.

112
00:08:46,401 --> 00:08:48,862
Someone who isn't a menace to society.

113
00:08:49,112 --> 00:08:50,155
Hmm…

114
00:08:51,156 --> 00:08:52,658
Someone who has a sound mind

115
00:08:52,741 --> 00:08:55,202
and… kind.

116
00:08:57,788 --> 00:09:00,540
She really thought
we couldn't afford bail, huh?

117
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:03,669
I'm really sorry for what happened.

118
00:09:04,419 --> 00:09:06,505
Patricia definitely overreacted.

119
00:09:06,797 --> 00:09:10,801
I thought she really needed the money.

120
00:09:11,927 --> 00:09:14,596
Make sure she doesn't
get a job ever again.

121
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:16,431
Oh, I'll guarantee you that.

122
00:09:17,099 --> 00:09:18,892
She wasted her big break.

123
00:09:19,309 --> 00:09:20,978
She crashed and burned
before anyone even knew her.

124
00:09:23,021 --> 00:09:25,482
But what happens to our case now?

125
00:09:26,316 --> 00:09:27,567
Don't worry.

126
00:09:28,485 --> 00:09:30,112
I have dirt on her.

127
00:09:31,029 --> 00:09:33,532
I still have the video we took of her.

128
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:39,579
All in.

129
00:09:40,455 --> 00:09:42,708
Let's see if she'd still press charges.

130
00:09:42,791 --> 00:09:44,126
It'd be her honor on the line.

131
00:09:49,506 --> 00:09:50,549
Seems you're lucky.

132
00:09:50,632 --> 00:09:53,427
-Yes!
-Good game.

133
00:10:00,392 --> 00:10:03,103
Uh, do you need anything?

134
00:10:03,186 --> 00:10:04,187
Ah, yes.

135
00:10:04,521 --> 00:10:07,941
All of Patricia's
audition footage is in there.

136
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:12,487
You've nothing to worry
about the producer and director.

137
00:10:13,238 --> 00:10:14,740
Why are you doing this?

138
00:10:15,198 --> 00:10:18,118
Part of my job
is to look after your image.

139
00:10:19,036 --> 00:10:20,245
It's my job to care.

140
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:22,581
And also because…

141
00:10:22,664 --> 00:10:24,624
Patricia doesn't deserve all that.

142
00:10:24,708 --> 00:10:26,126
But how did you get this?

143
00:10:26,209 --> 00:10:28,211
Diana, nothing is impossible.

144
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:32,049
Sometimes, we just have
to talk things out.

145
00:10:36,386 --> 00:10:37,679
What do you need from us?

146
00:10:37,929 --> 00:10:39,681
Where's Patricia's footage?

147
00:10:40,015 --> 00:10:41,308
We don't have it!

148
00:10:41,683 --> 00:10:45,312
-Agh!
-Please stop! Stop!

149
00:10:53,862 --> 00:10:55,113
Give it to me.

150
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:04,790
Where is it? Give it to me.

151
00:11:05,457 --> 00:11:06,833
Fine, I'll give it to you!

152
00:11:08,126 --> 00:11:10,087
I'll give it to you, just please stop!

153
00:11:10,921 --> 00:11:12,214
Please!

154
00:11:12,297 --> 00:11:14,091
That wasn't so hard, was it?

155
00:11:14,925 --> 00:11:16,343
We shouldn't have gone this far.

156
00:11:28,063 --> 00:11:29,398
I'll get going.

157
00:11:31,108 --> 00:11:32,651
Thank you for this.

158
00:11:36,738 --> 00:11:39,074
And for protecting Patricia.

159
00:11:40,075 --> 00:11:41,493
I appreciate it.

160
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:49,501
Is this you plan?

161
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:54,005
To be the next Mr. Aragon.

162
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:57,717
I thought you were the head of PR.

163
00:11:58,468 --> 00:11:59,886
I wasn't aware…

164
00:12:00,846 --> 00:12:02,347
that you're an aspiring gigolo

165
00:12:02,431 --> 00:12:04,766
and a gold digger on the side.

166
00:12:06,101 --> 00:12:08,353
Whatever you're doing,
it won't work on Diana.

167
00:12:09,438 --> 00:12:10,814
Martin already tried that.

168
00:12:11,106 --> 00:12:13,859
He gained her trust
and made her fall in love.

169
00:12:13,942 --> 00:12:15,193
But then what happened?

170
00:12:16,153 --> 00:12:18,822
She's too smart for antics.

171
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,035
-Interesting.
-It's very, very interesting.

172
00:12:24,119 --> 00:12:25,704
And if you do get her,

173
00:12:25,787 --> 00:12:27,706
and she allows you into her life,

174
00:12:28,039 --> 00:12:29,708
I doubt it'll last long.

175
00:12:30,667 --> 00:12:32,711
My sister doesn't know how to love.

176
00:12:32,961 --> 00:12:34,671
She will get tired of you.

177
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:39,551
All she's capable of loving
are La Familia and…

178
00:12:40,343 --> 00:12:41,344
herself.

179
00:12:44,306 --> 00:12:45,390
You're right.

180
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,977
Diana loves La Familia more than her life.

181
00:12:49,811 --> 00:12:53,648
What do you think
would she do to anyone who threatens it?

182
00:12:56,985 --> 00:12:58,403
Knowing Diana,

183
00:12:58,487 --> 00:13:00,614
she spares no one
when it comes to the company.

184
00:13:00,697 --> 00:13:02,199
Not her family…

185
00:13:04,367 --> 00:13:05,619
Not even her brother.

186
00:13:07,829 --> 00:13:09,539
I read the pitch for Burger City.

187
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:11,917
As the marketing head…

188
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:15,795
I need a complete sentiment analysis

189
00:13:16,505 --> 00:13:18,006
after the poisoning incident.

190
00:13:19,674 --> 00:13:21,051
Are you trying to boss me around?

191
00:13:22,511 --> 00:13:24,554
Have it ready by the end of the day, okay?

192
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:52,624
What's this?

193
00:13:53,291 --> 00:13:55,126
Schools with evening classes.

194
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:57,254
With flexible schedules.

195
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:59,172
So you can study while still working here.

196
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:03,802
Why are you giving me this?

197
00:14:04,594 --> 00:14:06,179
Ms. D asked me to.

198
00:14:06,263 --> 00:14:08,473
Is it because of
what happened the other day?

199
00:14:09,391 --> 00:14:11,935
Enzo, I won't give up on my dreams.

200
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,772
But Ms. D has a point, Patricia.

201
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:18,108
You almost got abused.

202
00:14:19,234 --> 00:14:23,029
Perhaps it's time
to look at your other options.

203
00:14:27,075 --> 00:14:28,285
But you know what…

204
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:31,746
not everyone is as bad as that director.

205
00:14:32,330 --> 00:14:36,334
I still believe there are good people
who will give me a chance.

206
00:14:37,335 --> 00:14:39,588
Don't take Ms. D's words the wrong way.

207
00:14:41,381 --> 00:14:43,758
She's trying to give you
a chance at a better life.

208
00:14:44,175 --> 00:14:47,262
If I do want to go back to school…

209
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:52,601
I will be the one deciding when and how.

210
00:14:53,226 --> 00:14:54,769
Not because it's what she wants.

211
00:14:55,437 --> 00:14:58,398
And most especially not
because I owe her anything.

212
00:14:58,857 --> 00:15:00,609
Is that how you really view
this situation?

213
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,988
She can keep ordering me around
in this company.

214
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:07,198
She can ask me to do everything!

215
00:15:07,949 --> 00:15:10,535
But only during my work hours here.

216
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:13,288
Outside of this building…

217
00:15:14,289 --> 00:15:15,999
I'm in control of my life.

218
00:15:16,541 --> 00:15:18,293
I get to decide…

219
00:15:18,877 --> 00:15:23,214
what I want for myself,
what I can give up.

220
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:28,887
None of you can tell me
what I should give up.

221
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:37,520
Ma'am, even just
a five-minute appointment is fine.

222
00:15:37,604 --> 00:15:40,106
Promise, that's all we need
for the elevator pitch.

223
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:43,068
I'm sorry, but the board's
schedule is packed.

224
00:15:43,151 --> 00:15:47,614
And the board has no more interest
to continue further with La Familia.

225
00:15:47,697 --> 00:15:50,408
Ma'am, what if we just talk to Mr. Smith?

226
00:15:50,659 --> 00:15:55,580
We're under strict rules not to entertain
any more proposals. I'm really sorry.

227
00:15:55,830 --> 00:15:58,875
Besides, Mr. Smith's not available today.

228
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,252
Why? Has he left the country?

229
00:16:01,878 --> 00:16:04,589
We're not allowed
to disclose that information.

230
00:16:06,424 --> 00:16:08,051
Patricia, this is over.

231
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:11,721
-We need to report to Ms. D.
-Huh? Wait, wait.

232
00:16:11,805 --> 00:16:13,723
What, we're giving up just like that?

233
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:16,434
Want me to sneak inside?
I'll find Mr. Smith.

234
00:16:16,685 --> 00:16:19,771
Patricia. Don't make a scene here.

235
00:16:19,854 --> 00:16:21,022
Fine!

236
00:16:22,357 --> 00:16:23,900
I'll just go pee.

237
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:26,986
-Fine. Make it quick.
-Yes.

238
00:16:27,070 --> 00:16:29,489
Uh, ma'am, can I use the restroom?

239
00:16:29,572 --> 00:16:31,700
-It's over there, ma'am.
-All right, thank you!

240
00:16:38,873 --> 00:16:40,750
Hello? Hi, hon!

241
00:16:41,751 --> 00:16:42,711
Yes, yes.

242
00:16:42,794 --> 00:16:45,380
Ah, I'm here. I'm here downstairs.

243
00:16:45,463 --> 00:16:47,132
I'll meet you at the parking lot.

244
00:16:47,215 --> 00:16:49,926
I'm excited. I can't wait
for this vacation,

245
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:51,636
even if it's just one night!

246
00:16:51,886 --> 00:16:55,390
I hear that Golden Sun Resort
is one of the best!

247
00:16:56,224 --> 00:16:59,477
Yes. I'll see you.
I'll see you, hon. Okay!

248
00:17:34,888 --> 00:17:36,139
What is it, Patricia?

249
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:40,643
Hey, hey! Where are you going?

250
00:17:41,686 --> 00:17:43,062
I'm not going to give up.

251
00:17:43,772 --> 00:17:45,815
Patricia, Mr. Smith's gone.

252
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:50,028
But that doesn't mean I'm out of options.

253
00:17:50,111 --> 00:17:52,655
If a door closes on you,
then go through the window.

254
00:17:52,739 --> 00:17:54,115
Ah, Enzo.

255
00:17:54,199 --> 00:17:56,785
Enzo, updates, please,
on what I asked you to do.

256
00:17:56,868 --> 00:17:59,204
Ms. D, Mr. Smith's already on vacation.

257
00:17:59,871 --> 00:18:01,080
Oh, my!

258
00:18:04,876 --> 00:18:07,253
Patricia, where are you going?

259
00:18:07,587 --> 00:18:09,464
I know where Mr. Smith is.

260
00:18:09,923 --> 00:18:11,674
I'll go and talk to him!

261
00:18:12,008 --> 00:18:14,135
No, no, no. You can't do that.

262
00:18:14,719 --> 00:18:17,055
Didn't you say
I should stop making excuses?

263
00:18:17,138 --> 00:18:18,890
This is me finding a way.

264
00:18:19,307 --> 00:18:21,684
But not this way! You cannot do that.

265
00:18:21,768 --> 00:18:23,102
-You cannot.
-Why not?

266
00:18:23,186 --> 00:18:25,438
That's not how we do things in business!

267
00:18:25,522 --> 00:18:27,065
That's very unprofessional.

268
00:18:31,319 --> 00:18:33,530
If you don't agree with what I'll do,

269
00:18:33,822 --> 00:18:35,657
then let me do it myself.

270
00:18:37,325 --> 00:18:38,827
No, no, no. Patricia.

271
00:18:39,661 --> 00:18:41,079
Patricia!

272
00:18:41,913 --> 00:18:43,164
Pat--

273
00:18:44,374 --> 00:18:47,752
-Call Benjie right now.
-Yes, Ms. D.

274
00:18:55,218 --> 00:18:57,095
Mr. Smith is not inside their room.

275
00:18:57,178 --> 00:18:59,430
Well, they're on vacation.
I guess they went out.

276
00:18:59,806 --> 00:19:01,266
-So--
-I'll look for them.

277
00:19:01,349 --> 00:19:03,518
-How? Where?
-Uh-- Ms. D.

278
00:19:05,854 --> 00:19:06,896
Diana!

279
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:09,065
Ms. Aragon! What are you doing here?

280
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:11,276
Um, if only we could have
a minute of your time.

281
00:19:11,359 --> 00:19:12,360
-For what?
-Ple--

282
00:19:12,694 --> 00:19:14,612
My company has already made

283
00:19:14,696 --> 00:19:15,947
-its decision.
-We understand,

284
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:17,407
but we went out of our way

285
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:19,158
-to meet you here.
-This is inappropriate!

286
00:19:19,659 --> 00:19:22,954
For you to come in here
like this unannounced,

287
00:19:23,037 --> 00:19:26,374
and ruined, frankly, my time off?

288
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:28,084
We know, we're sorry, but just one--

289
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:32,213
My company cannot work with La Familia!

290
00:19:32,839 --> 00:19:35,842
No means no!

291
00:19:44,809 --> 00:19:46,895
We did what you wanted. Let's go home.

292
00:19:46,978 --> 00:19:48,313
-But--
-Enough!

293
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:50,690
I've been humiliated enough!
We're going home.

294
00:19:50,982 --> 00:19:52,358
What's so funny?

295
00:19:53,151 --> 00:19:54,402
Uh…

296
00:19:55,028 --> 00:19:57,822
There's no denying
that she is your daughter.

297
00:19:57,906 --> 00:19:59,782
You're both stubborn.

298
00:20:03,786 --> 00:20:04,996
Just get in the car.

299
00:20:13,129 --> 00:20:15,548
Ma'am! Ma'am, are you okay?

300
00:20:15,632 --> 00:20:18,885
I need my medicine. I'm a diabetic.

301
00:20:18,968 --> 00:20:21,304
-Where is it? All right.
-In the car.

302
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:22,972
What-- What's happening?

303
00:20:23,056 --> 00:20:24,182
-What's wrong?
-She's dizzy.

304
00:20:24,265 --> 00:20:26,935
She needs to take her medicine. Wait.

305
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:31,814
-Oh!
-Oh, my goodness.

306
00:20:31,898 --> 00:20:33,274
Is there anything else you need, ma'am?

307
00:20:33,358 --> 00:20:35,109
I just need my medicine, please!

308
00:20:35,193 --> 00:20:37,195
-Where is it?
-At the back. White bag.

309
00:20:37,695 --> 00:20:38,863
Do you need water?

310
00:20:39,656 --> 00:20:40,865
Should I call anybody?

311
00:20:43,117 --> 00:20:45,244
-I think my husband
-Ms. D?

312
00:20:45,328 --> 00:20:46,788
-is somewhere here.
-I see.

313
00:20:46,871 --> 00:20:49,791
-So you're not driving? Okay.
-No, I can't.

314
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:56,673
-No, no. I just need to rest.
-Okay.

315
00:20:58,424 --> 00:20:59,467
Hon?

316
00:21:01,094 --> 00:21:02,303
What's happening here?

317
00:21:02,387 --> 00:21:03,972
Honey, they helped me.

318
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:08,267
We need to take her to the clinic.

319
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:12,397
Thank you for helping me.

320
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,898
No, don't mention it.

321
00:21:13,982 --> 00:21:15,191
Okay.

322
00:21:15,942 --> 00:21:18,403
I've been giving this some more thought.

323
00:21:18,903 --> 00:21:24,325
I don't like to see all the effort
that you've put into coming here wasted.

324
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:29,956
So, I'm giving you that chance to speak.

325
00:21:32,041 --> 00:21:37,046
Why are you so insistent
on pursuing this deal?

326
00:21:37,338 --> 00:21:40,258
Because this isn't just
another sales contract.

327
00:21:40,341 --> 00:21:42,927
This is going to change
the entire trajectory

328
00:21:43,011 --> 00:21:45,596
of both La Familia and Burger City.

329
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,765
Opportunities like this
don't just come around,

330
00:21:47,849 --> 00:21:49,100
Mr. Smith.

331
00:21:51,769 --> 00:21:54,022
Um, sir, if I may?

332
00:21:54,105 --> 00:21:55,273
Ms. D?

333
00:21:59,569 --> 00:22:02,155
The earliest memory I have…

334
00:22:03,531 --> 00:22:04,574
of my mother…

335
00:22:06,534 --> 00:22:08,036
is tied to Burger City.

336
00:22:09,704 --> 00:22:11,456
When I was six years old…

337
00:22:11,873 --> 00:22:14,917
my family and I went on a vacation abroad.

338
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:17,128
We ate at a Burger City there.

339
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:21,340
For a few days, I…

340
00:22:24,969 --> 00:22:26,262
…I got something

341
00:22:27,388 --> 00:22:28,973
I rarely had when I was growing up.

342
00:22:33,436 --> 00:22:34,812
She wasn't a boss.

343
00:22:34,896 --> 00:22:36,689
She wasn't an executive.

344
00:22:38,316 --> 00:22:39,859
She was just my mother.

345
00:22:50,578 --> 00:22:52,163
That's why, for me…

346
00:22:52,997 --> 00:22:55,708
La Familia and Burger City

347
00:22:56,292 --> 00:22:58,044
are always tied together.

348
00:23:00,421 --> 00:23:02,882
Because they will always remind me…

349
00:23:04,008 --> 00:23:05,843
of my time with my mother.

350
00:23:10,515 --> 00:23:13,851
We both celebrate families
and connections.

351
00:23:15,061 --> 00:23:17,855
It's safe to say that
we are the perfect pair.

352
00:23:26,531 --> 00:23:30,284
Look, I'll bring this up
with our other board members

353
00:23:30,368 --> 00:23:32,411
at the next management meeting.

354
00:23:33,079 --> 00:23:36,541
I cannot promise you anything.

355
00:23:38,251 --> 00:23:39,252
I think we must go.

356
00:23:39,877 --> 00:23:42,213
Thank you very much, Mr. Smith.

357
00:23:43,464 --> 00:23:44,924
Please think about it.

358
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,135
-I will.
-Thank you.

359
00:23:47,218 --> 00:23:48,553
-Thank you.
-Thank you again.

360
00:23:48,636 --> 00:23:50,805
-Thank you.
-Take care, ma'am. Thank you.

361
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:56,978
Wow, good job.

362
00:23:57,061 --> 00:23:58,437
Great story.

363
00:23:58,855 --> 00:24:00,064
Is it true?

364
00:24:06,779 --> 00:24:09,240
Oh, I just made up some parts.

365
00:24:09,657 --> 00:24:12,034
Don't forget, I'm an actor.

366
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:19,041
What is it?

367
00:24:19,750 --> 00:24:21,210
Thank you.

368
00:24:24,547 --> 00:24:25,840
You're welcome, Ms. D.

369
00:24:34,974 --> 00:24:36,809
I made you proud, Dad.

370
00:24:38,019 --> 00:24:40,938
It's like the universe was on our side.

371
00:24:42,023 --> 00:24:44,692
We've been trying to convince
this foreign investor

372
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:46,736
from Burger City.

373
00:24:47,361 --> 00:24:49,822
At first, he didn't even
want to talk to us.

374
00:24:50,239 --> 00:24:54,076
Then Mr. Smith's wife
had a diabetic emergency.

375
00:24:54,160 --> 00:24:56,162
So we helped her.

376
00:24:56,746 --> 00:24:58,623
Mr. Smith appreciated what we did.

377
00:24:58,706 --> 00:25:02,001
He gave us a chance
to present our proposal.

378
00:25:02,251 --> 00:25:05,796
It looks like you're enjoying your job.

379
00:25:07,048 --> 00:25:08,382
Not really.

380
00:25:09,091 --> 00:25:11,802
I'm just glad I did something right.

381
00:25:12,303 --> 00:25:13,888
You know, Patricia…

382
00:25:15,806 --> 00:25:19,060
you don't have to impress your mother.

383
00:25:19,727 --> 00:25:22,146
You won't be working
at La Familia for long.

384
00:25:25,358 --> 00:25:27,360
-Dad?
-Hmm?

385
00:25:27,693 --> 00:25:29,362
Why did you and Mom separate?

386
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:31,656
Huh?

387
00:25:31,989 --> 00:25:33,032
Where did that come from?

388
00:25:33,407 --> 00:25:35,076
You already know why.

389
00:25:36,244 --> 00:25:39,163
I know you two
fought a lot when I was a kid,

390
00:25:39,247 --> 00:25:40,665
but you never separated.

391
00:25:40,748 --> 00:25:44,460
What made you decide to end your marriage?

392
00:25:46,212 --> 00:25:47,964
Why are you asking me that?

393
00:25:50,341 --> 00:25:53,219
I'm trying to remember if…

394
00:25:56,264 --> 00:25:59,267
there was ever a time
when our family was happy.

395
00:26:00,268 --> 00:26:03,729
Because all I remember is the pain.

396
00:26:04,105 --> 00:26:07,191
That pain you remember…

397
00:26:08,484 --> 00:26:09,986
was because of your mother.

398
00:26:10,569 --> 00:26:11,821
Remember,

399
00:26:12,321 --> 00:26:13,990
she abandoned us.

400
00:26:14,282 --> 00:26:16,158
I don't want you to go through that again.

401
00:26:23,958 --> 00:26:25,918
-You called for me?
-Mm-hmm.

402
00:26:26,002 --> 00:26:27,962
We've heard from Burger City.

403
00:26:30,214 --> 00:26:33,301
Ms. D wants you to be here
when she reads the email.

404
00:26:33,384 --> 00:26:35,594
Okay, Enzo. Show us.

405
00:26:41,058 --> 00:26:42,268
Let me read it.

406
00:26:42,977 --> 00:26:44,395
"Dear Ms. Diana Aragon,

407
00:26:44,478 --> 00:26:46,147
your passion and commitment are evident,

408
00:26:46,230 --> 00:26:48,482
and we truly appreciate
the effort you've invested

409
00:26:48,566 --> 00:26:50,985
in presenting this
partnership opportunity.

410
00:26:51,277 --> 00:26:52,778
After careful consideration,

411
00:26:52,862 --> 00:26:57,366
we are pleased to explore
this partnership further.

412
00:26:57,616 --> 00:27:01,912
We believe there are a few final points
that will still require our mutual review,

413
00:27:01,996 --> 00:27:06,667
but we are fully open to discussions
to finalize the details.

414
00:27:06,751 --> 00:27:09,754
We look forward to building
a successful collaboration

415
00:27:09,837 --> 00:27:12,381
with La Familia Beverages Corporation.

416
00:27:12,465 --> 00:27:14,508
Sincerely, Jonathan Smith,

417
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:18,804
President and CEO
of Burger City Foods Inc."

418
00:27:19,138 --> 00:27:20,348
Yes!

419
00:27:21,724 --> 00:27:23,351
Yes!

420
00:27:23,684 --> 00:27:26,062
-Yes!
-Congratulations, everyone.

421
00:27:26,145 --> 00:27:27,355
-Congrats to us.
-We did it!

422
00:27:31,108 --> 00:27:32,735
Congratulations.

423
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:33,819
Great job.

424
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:43,245
The meeting with Burger City went great.

425
00:27:43,621 --> 00:27:44,789
This is our second chance,

426
00:27:44,872 --> 00:27:46,248
so let's not waste it.

427
00:27:46,749 --> 00:27:49,710
This time, I want everything done right.

428
00:27:50,711 --> 00:27:53,964
Teddy, prepare the marketing
strategies immediately.

429
00:27:54,048 --> 00:27:55,800
We'll set another meeting for that.

430
00:27:57,009 --> 00:27:59,720
Patricia, you help
with initial market research.

431
00:28:01,138 --> 00:28:03,808
Enzo, legal. Coordinate with them.

432
00:28:03,891 --> 00:28:05,976
I want to see the first draft
of the contract

433
00:28:06,060 --> 00:28:07,728
on my table this afternoon.

434
00:28:08,187 --> 00:28:09,355
Already on it, Ms. D.

435
00:28:11,732 --> 00:28:14,026
What is the state
of the company's finances?

436
00:28:14,110 --> 00:28:17,196
Will we be able to support
Burger City's future plans?

437
00:28:17,571 --> 00:28:19,865
We can support the expansion, Ms. D.

438
00:28:19,949 --> 00:28:21,617
But not without adjustments.

439
00:28:21,951 --> 00:28:27,206
The food poisoning issue
heavily affected the sales of Cala Soda.

440
00:28:27,289 --> 00:28:30,334
Right now, we are still
recovering our losses

441
00:28:30,543 --> 00:28:33,087
while maintaining operating costs.

442
00:28:33,921 --> 00:28:35,464
If we want to accommodate

443
00:28:35,548 --> 00:28:38,384
the future demands of Burger City,

444
00:28:38,759 --> 00:28:41,512
the company needs
to generate additional revenue

445
00:28:42,096 --> 00:28:44,390
or reduce expenses.

446
00:28:45,808 --> 00:28:49,937
Or we can lay off some employees, right?

447
00:28:51,313 --> 00:28:53,607
The company has too many employees.

448
00:28:53,691 --> 00:28:56,569
So, if we lay off some of them,

449
00:28:56,861 --> 00:28:58,988
we'll definitely reduce our expenses.

450
00:28:59,196 --> 00:29:00,281
Don't you agree?

451
00:29:02,950 --> 00:29:04,034
I agree.

452
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:09,373
However, we can't sacrifice our employees.

453
00:29:11,083 --> 00:29:13,627
This building is costing us
more than it should.

454
00:29:14,253 --> 00:29:16,005
We are going to sell this building.

455
00:29:16,088 --> 00:29:19,049
We'll relocate to the former
headquarters of La Familia.

456
00:29:19,467 --> 00:29:20,968
If we do that,

457
00:29:21,218 --> 00:29:23,846
we will greatly reduce our expenses.

458
00:29:24,221 --> 00:29:25,681
Besides,

459
00:29:26,182 --> 00:29:29,018
I think it's time we brought
La Familia back home.

460
00:29:34,106 --> 00:29:35,232
Dismissed.

461
00:29:42,364 --> 00:29:44,658
Did you get all the files from marketing?

462
00:29:44,742 --> 00:29:47,369
-Pull out everything.
-Where should I put this, sir?

463
00:29:47,453 --> 00:29:48,662
Please put it in Ms. D's office.

464
00:29:48,746 --> 00:29:49,955
Thank you.

465
00:29:50,247 --> 00:29:51,957
Everyone, everyone, listen!

466
00:29:52,041 --> 00:29:55,294
We need to sort everything out, okay?

467
00:29:55,377 --> 00:29:56,670
After Ms. D's meeting,

468
00:29:56,754 --> 00:29:58,923
she's going to head here. Understood?

469
00:29:59,006 --> 00:30:00,883
-Yes, sir.
-Thank you.

470
00:30:02,343 --> 00:30:03,385
My gosh!

471
00:30:12,561 --> 00:30:13,562
You're still here?

472
00:30:14,438 --> 00:30:15,814
Yes. Are you going home?

473
00:30:15,898 --> 00:30:17,483
This early? That's unlike you.

474
00:30:17,566 --> 00:30:19,568
One of those rare moments.

475
00:30:20,694 --> 00:30:22,112
You're taking work home?

476
00:30:22,488 --> 00:30:24,365
I wouldn't be able to sleep anyway.

477
00:30:28,702 --> 00:30:29,954
What's that?

478
00:30:30,037 --> 00:30:32,373
This is what I take when I can't sleep.

479
00:30:32,915 --> 00:30:34,792
You know, this needs to rest too.

480
00:30:36,627 --> 00:30:38,295
It's hard to be alone.

481
00:30:38,379 --> 00:30:42,925
The worst part is when you're
already lying in bed…

482
00:30:43,384 --> 00:30:45,594
but you can't sleep
because you have a lot on your mind.

483
00:30:45,886 --> 00:30:47,429
All your problems…

484
00:30:47,805 --> 00:30:49,473
everything you’re going through,

485
00:30:49,557 --> 00:30:51,016
so many regrets.

486
00:30:51,267 --> 00:30:54,853
Take it so you can rest.

487
00:30:56,272 --> 00:30:58,148
Thank you?

488
00:31:03,028 --> 00:31:04,029
So--

489
00:31:04,113 --> 00:31:05,239
Oh!

490
00:31:08,701 --> 00:31:09,702
I'm sorry.

491
00:31:15,416 --> 00:31:16,500
Thank you.

492
00:31:17,835 --> 00:31:19,086
Rest well, Ms. Aragon.

493
00:31:19,837 --> 00:31:20,838
Good night.

494
00:31:21,964 --> 00:31:23,007
Good night.

495
00:31:58,417 --> 00:32:00,628
-Okay.
-Thank you again, Mr. Smith.

496
00:32:00,711 --> 00:32:02,004
-Thanks for coming by.
-Thank you so much.

497
00:32:02,087 --> 00:32:03,547
I look forward to our next meeting.

498
00:32:03,631 --> 00:32:04,965
As do I. Thank you.

499
00:32:05,049 --> 00:32:06,300
-Okay.
-Mm-hmm.

500
00:32:08,719 --> 00:32:09,803
Ms. D.

501
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:15,267
We have a lot to prepare

502
00:32:15,351 --> 00:32:18,062
for La Familia's partnership
with Burger City.

503
00:32:18,145 --> 00:32:22,399
So you need to clear out
a quarter of our office

504
00:32:22,483 --> 00:32:25,653
because they're going
to need offices inside La Familia.

505
00:32:26,445 --> 00:32:27,696
The partnership will push through?

506
00:32:27,988 --> 00:32:31,200
Yes. We don't have any problems anymore
because everything has been cleared

507
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:35,454
and they value our competence
more than the rumors.

508
00:32:35,746 --> 00:32:37,164
So get to work.

509
00:32:37,247 --> 00:32:39,124
Make sure everything is prepared.

510
00:32:39,583 --> 00:32:40,876
Yes, Ms. D.

511
00:32:41,335 --> 00:32:42,628
Yes!

512
00:32:44,380 --> 00:32:45,631
Wait.

513
00:32:51,220 --> 00:32:52,262
Thank you.

514
00:32:56,975 --> 00:32:58,936
Patricia helped me out in this, Ms. D.

515
00:33:03,357 --> 00:33:04,525
Thank you.

516
00:33:05,526 --> 00:33:07,528
All the years you've spent
training under me

517
00:33:07,611 --> 00:33:09,071
didn't go to waste.

518
00:33:09,488 --> 00:33:11,824
You've made me so proud, Enzo.

519
00:33:14,368 --> 00:33:15,619
Thank you, Ms. D.

520
00:33:17,413 --> 00:33:18,747
You can go.

521
00:33:19,415 --> 00:33:21,166
You've been smiling since earlier.

522
00:33:23,168 --> 00:33:25,504
See? You're still smiling.

523
00:33:27,798 --> 00:33:28,841
I'm just happy.

524
00:33:28,924 --> 00:33:30,801
Because Ms. D complimented you?

525
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:35,973
Well, I can't relate to that.

526
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:38,350
Huh?

527
00:33:38,434 --> 00:33:40,018
She thanked you, too.

528
00:33:40,602 --> 00:33:43,272
Come on, she appreciates you.

529
00:33:43,689 --> 00:33:45,274
I remember when I was a kid…

530
00:33:47,401 --> 00:33:49,445
all I heard from her was…

531
00:33:51,864 --> 00:33:52,865
What?

532
00:33:53,282 --> 00:33:55,159
-"Patricia, don't."
-What?

533
00:33:55,242 --> 00:33:57,161
-"Patricia, stop doing that!"
-Huh?

534
00:33:57,244 --> 00:33:59,079
"Patricia, you're so stubborn!"

535
00:33:59,788 --> 00:34:00,622
Those things.

536
00:34:01,582 --> 00:34:02,666
What?

537
00:34:02,750 --> 00:34:05,586
Why? It's true, isn't it? You're stubborn.

538
00:34:06,712 --> 00:34:08,839
Besides, aren't all mothers like that?

539
00:34:10,007 --> 00:34:12,259
Well, yes, but…

540
00:34:13,469 --> 00:34:16,013
Have I never done anything right?

541
00:34:16,638 --> 00:34:17,765
Hmm?

542
00:34:21,477 --> 00:34:22,770
Did you know…

543
00:34:24,438 --> 00:34:28,108
when I was a kid, after my parents died,

544
00:34:28,525 --> 00:34:30,235
I lived with my aunt.

545
00:34:30,694 --> 00:34:33,405
But my aunt was young,
so she wasn't home most of the time.

546
00:34:33,489 --> 00:34:34,782
She had to work.

547
00:34:35,073 --> 00:34:37,451
So the people in La Familia…

548
00:34:37,534 --> 00:34:39,203
became my guardians.

549
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:43,540
All the people my mom and dad worked with…

550
00:34:45,167 --> 00:34:48,253
They took turns bringing me
to and from school.

551
00:34:48,879 --> 00:34:50,714
Some of them even gave me an allowance.

552
00:34:50,798 --> 00:34:52,216
And Ms. D?

553
00:34:52,299 --> 00:34:55,928
Ms. D was always present
during my school activities.

554
00:34:57,137 --> 00:35:00,015
She was the one who accompanied me
during my graduation.

555
00:35:03,435 --> 00:35:05,646
It's impossible for me to relate to that.

556
00:35:11,318 --> 00:35:12,361
I'm sorry.

557
00:35:15,447 --> 00:35:17,491
He also had a huge debt before.

558
00:35:18,784 --> 00:35:20,285
I knew it.

559
00:35:20,786 --> 00:35:22,204
He's after Diana's money.

560
00:35:22,287 --> 00:35:23,914
That's why he's trying
to get close to her.

561
00:35:25,707 --> 00:35:26,792
Great.

562
00:35:31,380 --> 00:35:33,799
Let's see if he can still
get close to her…

563
00:35:35,259 --> 00:35:37,511
now that I have a card
to play against him.

564
00:35:41,265 --> 00:35:44,393
I don't think anyone wins
in your betting game.

565
00:35:44,476 --> 00:35:45,978
-You'll be the first one.
-Eat up.

566
00:35:46,061 --> 00:35:47,396
-You'll be the first one.
-Oh, Patricia.

567
00:35:48,230 --> 00:35:49,231
Oliver.

568
00:35:49,648 --> 00:35:51,859
-Come.
-Uh, Dad.

569
00:35:53,443 --> 00:35:55,153
Good thing you're home.

570
00:35:56,446 --> 00:35:57,698
Why? What's going on?

571
00:35:57,781 --> 00:35:59,366
It's your mother.

572
00:36:00,075 --> 00:36:01,368
She wanted to treat us.

573
00:36:01,451 --> 00:36:03,412
Go inside. You should eat.

574
00:36:03,495 --> 00:36:04,997
Oliver, go inside.

575
00:36:06,456 --> 00:36:07,541
Mm…

576
00:36:08,709 --> 00:36:10,210
Dig in. There's a lot of food.

577
00:36:10,294 --> 00:36:12,963
-It's so good!
-Sis, join us! It's good!

578
00:36:13,046 --> 00:36:14,047
Hmm…

579
00:36:14,298 --> 00:36:15,924
That food looks good, bestie.

580
00:36:17,259 --> 00:36:18,093
Mom.

581
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:19,845
What's the occasion?

582
00:36:21,471 --> 00:36:23,807
Just a little celebration

583
00:36:24,308 --> 00:36:26,393
because I finally got a job.

584
00:36:27,561 --> 00:36:28,604
Really, Mom?

585
00:36:28,687 --> 00:36:29,938
Yes.

586
00:36:31,523 --> 00:36:33,358
Where did you get the money to buy these?

587
00:36:33,609 --> 00:36:35,611
I took a portion of our rent.

588
00:36:35,694 --> 00:36:37,112
But don't worry.

589
00:36:37,195 --> 00:36:39,823
Once I get my first salary,
I'll pay it back double.

590
00:36:40,324 --> 00:36:42,910
What job is it? Where's your office?

591
00:36:42,993 --> 00:36:46,121
Uh, I'll be a company secretary.

592
00:36:46,204 --> 00:36:49,333
But I'm still taking care
of the requirements.

593
00:36:49,416 --> 00:36:52,169
Don't worry. I'll tell you soon.

594
00:36:53,253 --> 00:36:54,838
There's a surprise element, huh?

595
00:36:54,922 --> 00:36:55,839
Mm-hmm.

596
00:36:55,923 --> 00:36:58,008
Sis, sit down. Let's eat.

597
00:36:58,467 --> 00:37:00,010
-Come on. It's good!
-Bestie, sit over there.

598
00:37:00,093 --> 00:37:01,094
Mm.

599
00:37:02,846 --> 00:37:05,933
I want a complete audit
of the PR Department.

600
00:37:06,558 --> 00:37:10,354
All expenses, reimbursements.
All transactions.

601
00:37:10,854 --> 00:37:13,899
Sir, that would need Ms. D's approval.

602
00:37:13,982 --> 00:37:15,817
What approval are you talking about?

603
00:37:16,193 --> 00:37:18,403
PR is under Marketing.

604
00:37:19,488 --> 00:37:22,991
Am I not allowed to know
what's happening in my own department?

605
00:37:25,494 --> 00:37:26,745
Just do it.

606
00:37:27,037 --> 00:37:28,872
I have my suspicions about Ricardo.

607
00:37:28,956 --> 00:37:30,332
He's riddled with debt.

608
00:37:31,625 --> 00:37:32,876
All right.

609
00:37:34,127 --> 00:37:36,088
I want everything confidential for now.

610
00:37:36,838 --> 00:37:37,965
I'll take care of Diana.

611
00:37:58,110 --> 00:38:00,153
Yes, I'm coming.

612
00:38:00,946 --> 00:38:03,657
I'm sorry. I only had time just now.

613
00:38:04,241 --> 00:38:05,409
Yes, I have the payment.

614
00:38:06,326 --> 00:38:07,828
I'll give it to you, all right?

615
00:39:50,305 --> 00:39:52,349
Isabelle Chavez…

616
00:39:54,226 --> 00:39:55,977
Why are you following me?

617
00:40:12,077 --> 00:40:15,539
Uh, Diana? You wanted to talk to me?

618
00:40:20,752 --> 00:40:22,087
Explain yourself.

619
00:40:24,798 --> 00:40:27,843
How will we trust people like that?

620
00:40:28,677 --> 00:40:32,013
Think about it.
What if the people you're involved with

621
00:40:32,097 --> 00:40:33,932
suddenly cause trouble here?

622
00:40:35,142 --> 00:40:37,435
We don't deal with these kinds of people.

623
00:40:37,727 --> 00:40:38,854
Is it true?

624
00:40:40,564 --> 00:40:41,773
Yes.

625
00:40:42,315 --> 00:40:45,986
But that's outside of my job
here at La Familia.

626
00:40:46,069 --> 00:40:47,154
Oh, no.

627
00:40:49,322 --> 00:40:52,075
The company policy has a morality clause.

628
00:40:53,702 --> 00:40:56,663
Diana, that happened
before I was even employed here.

629
00:40:56,746 --> 00:40:58,748
I am not stealing from your company.

630
00:40:58,832 --> 00:41:01,418
Well, should we wait
for something to happen?

631
00:41:02,335 --> 00:41:05,505
People addicted to gambling are dangerous.

632
00:41:06,006 --> 00:41:07,465
They spare nothing and no one,

633
00:41:07,549 --> 00:41:09,050
especially when they're desperate.

634
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:14,723
I am not doing anything wrong.

635
00:41:17,017 --> 00:41:18,476
But Teddy's right.

636
00:41:19,477 --> 00:41:21,730
This is too much of a liability.

637
00:41:22,147 --> 00:41:25,775
Now, you're vulnerable
to blackmail, bribery, whatever.

638
00:41:26,151 --> 00:41:29,237
And your contract has a morality clause.

639
00:41:33,033 --> 00:41:34,826
Sir Ricardo, tell them the truth.

640
00:41:36,369 --> 00:41:37,370
Patricia.

641
00:41:38,038 --> 00:41:39,748
Patricia, this has nothing to do with you.

642
00:41:40,081 --> 00:41:43,710
Of course. Fine, team up.

643
00:41:45,420 --> 00:41:49,132
You're judging him for a mistake
he made in the past.

644
00:41:49,758 --> 00:41:51,009
Yes, he has debts.

645
00:41:51,843 --> 00:41:53,178
Yes, he gambled.

646
00:41:54,012 --> 00:41:55,639
But he only did all that…

647
00:41:56,264 --> 00:41:59,059
so he could pay
for his daughter's cancer treatment.

648
00:41:59,392 --> 00:42:00,477
Patricia.

649
00:42:01,811 --> 00:42:03,271
Sorry, Sir Ricardo.

650
00:42:03,355 --> 00:42:04,773
They have to know.

651
00:42:06,483 --> 00:42:08,652
You don't know what it feels like

652
00:42:08,735 --> 00:42:12,072
to be desperate
just to save the person you love.

653
00:42:14,991 --> 00:42:17,911
Why should this define him as a person?

654
00:42:18,245 --> 00:42:22,958
He did so much for the company,
yet you do this to him?

655
00:42:23,333 --> 00:42:25,001
Oh, my god. What is this?

656
00:42:25,418 --> 00:42:27,170
Diana, what is this? I can't believe--

657
00:42:27,254 --> 00:42:29,214
What kind of emotional
manipulation is this?

658
00:42:29,297 --> 00:42:31,549
Is Patricia telling the truth?

659
00:42:34,970 --> 00:42:36,096
Uh, yes.

660
00:42:38,223 --> 00:42:39,557
Oh, my god, Diana…

661
00:42:42,852 --> 00:42:43,895
Teddy…

662
00:42:46,273 --> 00:42:48,149
How did you get these pictures?

663
00:42:51,778 --> 00:42:55,907
Did you have someone spy
on one of the company's executives?

664
00:42:57,367 --> 00:42:58,451
Teddy?

665
00:42:59,327 --> 00:43:00,495
I was…

666
00:43:00,829 --> 00:43:01,955
trying…

667
00:43:02,706 --> 00:43:04,165
to think of the company.

668
00:43:05,625 --> 00:43:07,377
All of you, get out of my office.

669
00:43:53,298 --> 00:43:54,341
Are you going home?

670
00:43:54,758 --> 00:43:57,594
Why didn't you tell me
about your daughter?

671
00:43:58,136 --> 00:44:00,722
I will never exploit my daughter's memory

672
00:44:00,805 --> 00:44:02,390
to defend myself.

673
00:44:02,807 --> 00:44:04,976
I refuse to run away from my obligation.

674
00:44:05,685 --> 00:44:07,604
Every debt must be paid.

675
00:44:09,981 --> 00:44:11,649
I don't expect you to understand.

676
00:44:12,609 --> 00:44:15,612
To do something wrong
just to save your child?

677
00:44:17,155 --> 00:44:18,823
I understand.

678
00:44:31,878 --> 00:44:34,506
Make sure this doesn't affect your job.

679
00:44:36,925 --> 00:44:39,010
Aren't you going to fire me?

680
00:44:39,677 --> 00:44:42,764
Don't give me a reason to fire you.

681
00:45:28,852 --> 00:45:30,562
So it all backfired on you?

682
00:45:30,645 --> 00:45:32,105
In the end, he became the victim.

683
00:45:32,188 --> 00:45:33,982
All because Patricia came to his rescue.

684
00:45:34,941 --> 00:45:36,693
He'll get what's coming to him someday.

685
00:45:40,780 --> 00:45:42,615
Hey! Are you blind?

686
00:45:42,991 --> 00:45:45,201
Sir, someone wanted you to have this.

687
00:45:59,090 --> 00:46:00,925
Patricia, I assume
the office floor is ready

688
00:46:01,009 --> 00:46:02,886
for the Burger City transition team?

689
00:46:03,386 --> 00:46:05,054
They'll only be here temporarily,

690
00:46:05,138 --> 00:46:07,682
but they'll serve
as our communication channel.

691
00:46:07,765 --> 00:46:10,185
So all concerns, requests,
and coordination

692
00:46:10,268 --> 00:46:11,394
must go through them.

693
00:46:12,645 --> 00:46:14,314
Understood. All good, sir.

694
00:46:14,898 --> 00:46:17,525
Okay. I think Mr. Borja
and his team are arriving soon.

695
00:46:17,775 --> 00:46:18,902
Okay.

696
00:46:31,331 --> 00:46:32,582
Good afternoon, Mr. Borja.

697
00:46:32,665 --> 00:46:34,292
-Good afternoon.
-This is Patricia.

698
00:46:34,375 --> 00:46:36,044
-Oh, it's nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you as well.

699
00:46:36,127 --> 00:46:37,962
We can now proceed to your office floor.

700
00:46:38,046 --> 00:46:40,173
So is everything ready
for our event tonight?

701
00:46:40,256 --> 00:46:42,258
Yes, Patricia and I
double checked everything.

702
00:46:42,342 --> 00:46:43,551
Perfect. Let's go.

703
00:46:43,635 --> 00:46:45,011
Okay, let me escort you to your office.

704
00:46:45,094 --> 00:46:46,679
-All right.
-Welcome.

705
00:46:48,640 --> 00:46:50,016
Hello!

706
00:46:50,099 --> 00:46:52,477
Surprise!

707
00:46:55,104 --> 00:46:56,314
Mom…

708
00:46:57,565 --> 00:46:59,400
What are you doing here?

709
00:47:00,443 --> 00:47:03,446
Didn't I tell you I've got a new job?

710
00:47:03,530 --> 00:47:04,656
This is it!

711
00:47:05,907 --> 00:47:08,284
I'm back in the corporate world.

712
00:47:08,368 --> 00:47:10,870
I've been assigned as the secretary

713
00:47:10,954 --> 00:47:12,956
of Burger City's transition team.

714
00:47:13,248 --> 00:47:14,290
Look at this.

715
00:47:16,042 --> 00:47:19,045
So you have prior experience
working as a secretary?

716
00:47:19,128 --> 00:47:21,965
Since I already worked at La Familia,

717
00:47:22,048 --> 00:47:24,926
I know everything that needs to be done

718
00:47:25,009 --> 00:47:27,178
as an executive secretary.

719
00:47:29,597 --> 00:47:31,891
But that was years ago.

720
00:47:32,308 --> 00:47:33,685
Um…

721
00:47:34,143 --> 00:47:38,189
By the way, my daughter,
Patricia, works there.

722
00:47:38,648 --> 00:47:41,693
If I may, Mr. Smith.

723
00:47:42,026 --> 00:47:43,027
Um…

724
00:47:43,111 --> 00:47:45,863
I've heard a lot of good things about you.

725
00:47:46,447 --> 00:47:47,574
From whom?

726
00:47:47,657 --> 00:47:49,617
Patricia Aragon, my daughter.

727
00:47:51,911 --> 00:47:55,248
Isn't she the daughter
of La Familia's CEO?

728
00:47:55,665 --> 00:47:56,874
She's the one who saved your wife.

729
00:47:58,418 --> 00:48:01,337
Yes, that Patricia!

730
00:48:01,838 --> 00:48:04,757
She considers me her mom

731
00:48:04,841 --> 00:48:10,555
because I raised her
since she was very young

732
00:48:10,638 --> 00:48:13,308
and taught her everything
she needs to know.

733
00:48:13,391 --> 00:48:16,686
If she's Diana Aragon's daughter…

734
00:48:17,353 --> 00:48:19,480
why don't you just ask for help
from your daughter

735
00:48:19,564 --> 00:48:21,065
so you can get back to La Familia?

736
00:48:21,149 --> 00:48:26,154
I don't want to use my daughter
to get a job.

737
00:48:26,237 --> 00:48:28,531
I don't do that, sir, because…

738
00:48:29,115 --> 00:48:32,243
of course, I'm protecting my daughter.

739
00:48:32,327 --> 00:48:34,078
Just like a good mother should.

740
00:48:34,954 --> 00:48:36,456
You raised a good daughter.

741
00:48:38,249 --> 00:48:40,376
I know, right, sir?

742
00:48:42,795 --> 00:48:46,758
Come on, Patricia. Don't you trust me?

743
00:48:47,258 --> 00:48:50,470
Oh, no. It's not like that.

744
00:48:50,553 --> 00:48:53,056
I'm just surprised.

745
00:48:53,389 --> 00:48:56,351
Anyway, let's talk later.

746
00:48:56,434 --> 00:48:58,895
Where's our office?

747
00:49:00,438 --> 00:49:01,606
It's this way.

748
00:49:01,689 --> 00:49:03,066
-Let's go.
-Okay.

749
00:49:03,566 --> 00:49:04,817
-Mr. Smith.
-Ms. Aragon.

750
00:49:04,901 --> 00:49:06,277
It's finally happening.

751
00:49:06,361 --> 00:49:07,987
Ms. Aragon, this is wonderful.

752
00:49:08,071 --> 00:49:09,072
Dear Patricia.

753
00:49:09,155 --> 00:49:10,823
-Remember my daughter?
-I do, indeed.

754
00:49:10,907 --> 00:49:12,533
-Thank you again.
-Nice to see you again, sir.

755
00:49:12,617 --> 00:49:14,661
Sir, please make yourselves at home.

756
00:49:14,744 --> 00:49:16,162
-Thank you.
-This is your table.

757
00:49:16,245 --> 00:49:18,456
Hello. Welcome. Please.

758
00:49:18,998 --> 00:49:20,625
You attend to Mr. Smith.

759
00:49:20,708 --> 00:49:22,001
Yes, Ms. D.

760
00:49:22,752 --> 00:49:24,003
Diana.

761
00:49:24,087 --> 00:49:25,463
Hi. I'm sorry, I'm late.

762
00:49:25,546 --> 00:49:27,256
I just escorted our media partners here.

763
00:49:27,340 --> 00:49:30,176
I also brought in more content creators
to cover the event.

764
00:49:30,259 --> 00:49:31,344
Oh, good.

765
00:49:44,607 --> 00:49:47,193
Carlota, what are you doing here?

766
00:49:48,903 --> 00:49:49,946
Uh…

767
00:49:50,405 --> 00:49:54,492
You haven't told her yet, Patricia?

768
00:49:55,702 --> 00:50:00,790
I'm one of the secretaries
working for Burger City.

769
00:50:00,873 --> 00:50:03,334
What's the catch, Carlota?

770
00:50:03,418 --> 00:50:05,294
I know you're planning something.

771
00:50:06,796 --> 00:50:09,090
Aw, Ms. D…

772
00:50:10,299 --> 00:50:13,344
Don't be so suspicious.

773
00:50:13,428 --> 00:50:16,097
We're all professionals here.

774
00:50:16,180 --> 00:50:19,976
Let's try to work together.

775
00:50:20,351 --> 00:50:22,270
We don't really have a choice.

776
00:50:22,353 --> 00:50:24,147
Whether we like it or not…

777
00:50:25,148 --> 00:50:27,775
we're going to be working together.

778
00:50:28,317 --> 00:50:30,194
I can handle it.

779
00:50:30,278 --> 00:50:31,946
Can you?

780
00:50:35,742 --> 00:50:36,951
You're right.

781
00:50:37,618 --> 00:50:39,162
This is professional.

782
00:50:39,537 --> 00:50:43,082
So I expect you won't cause any trouble.

783
00:50:43,875 --> 00:50:45,042
Of course.

784
00:50:45,877 --> 00:50:47,545
Mr. Borja!

785
00:50:48,296 --> 00:50:50,214
-Hi, Mr. Smith.
-Oh, hi.

786
00:50:54,677 --> 00:50:55,803
Ms. D…

787
00:50:56,637 --> 00:50:59,557
Why didn't you tell me about Carlota?

788
00:51:01,058 --> 00:51:03,060
I'm sorry. I got busy.

789
00:51:03,895 --> 00:51:07,523
I only found out
she'd be working for Burger City earlier.

790
00:51:09,275 --> 00:51:11,694
She's been looking
for a job for a long time

791
00:51:11,986 --> 00:51:13,446
so she could help around the house.

792
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:14,989
Come on.

793
00:51:15,990 --> 00:51:19,452
You know Carlota and I
aren't on good terms.

794
00:51:20,870 --> 00:51:22,497
Not really, to be honest.

795
00:51:24,081 --> 00:51:26,542
What exactly happened between you and Mom?

796
00:51:28,419 --> 00:51:31,005
Why do you despise each other so much?

797
00:51:31,088 --> 00:51:34,967
Didn't she and Dad get together
only after you two separated?

798
00:51:37,929 --> 00:51:39,639
Is that what they told you?

799
00:51:41,557 --> 00:51:44,310
We don't really talk about it at home.

800
00:51:44,393 --> 00:51:45,728
That's all I know.

801
00:51:48,231 --> 00:51:49,357
Patricia.

802
00:51:52,068 --> 00:51:53,194
Dad?

803
00:51:55,947 --> 00:51:56,989
Dad.

804
00:51:58,616 --> 00:51:59,951
Martin!

805
00:52:02,245 --> 00:52:04,455
I've been waiting for you.

806
00:52:05,122 --> 00:52:06,582
Traffic was bad.

807
00:52:07,124 --> 00:52:08,584
Are you sure I'm allowed to be here?

808
00:52:08,668 --> 00:52:10,920
Of course.
I already got my boss's permission.

809
00:52:11,003 --> 00:52:13,965
There are so many
potential business partners here.

810
00:52:14,048 --> 00:52:15,758
Look.

811
00:52:17,426 --> 00:52:18,594
Don't look at them.

812
00:52:18,678 --> 00:52:20,972
Just relax before you go onstage.

813
00:52:21,764 --> 00:52:24,100
And now, to kick off our launch,

814
00:52:24,183 --> 00:52:28,145
let's hear some words
from the unbeatable, the unsinkable

815
00:52:28,229 --> 00:52:30,022
Diana Aragon!

816
00:52:41,033 --> 00:52:42,243
Thank you.

817
00:52:49,542 --> 00:52:53,212
Dear friends, esteemed executives,

818
00:52:53,296 --> 00:52:55,715
shareholders, and family,

819
00:52:56,048 --> 00:52:58,050
a pleasant evening to all of you.

820
00:52:59,135 --> 00:53:04,098
We have faced many challenges
these past months.

821
00:53:04,765 --> 00:53:08,561
But as they say,
you cannot put good people down.

822
00:53:08,644 --> 00:53:12,481
As we open this new chapter today

823
00:53:12,732 --> 00:53:14,358
with Burger City,

824
00:53:14,859 --> 00:53:18,863
who placed their trust in us
even through the storm,

825
00:53:19,488 --> 00:53:22,491
we're sincerely grateful
for your trust and confidence.

826
00:53:34,128 --> 00:53:37,882
And so, as we move forward
with this new partnership,

827
00:53:37,965 --> 00:53:40,009
we are proud to present to you…

828
00:53:40,259 --> 00:53:42,678
the vision of this partnership.

829
00:53:58,027 --> 00:53:59,153
Stop! Stop-- Stop.

830
00:53:59,236 --> 00:54:00,821
Stop this video! Stop this video!

831
00:54:00,905 --> 00:54:01,948
Stop it!

832
00:54:16,837 --> 00:54:17,880
Ms. D!

833
00:54:18,339 --> 00:54:19,632
Ms. D!

834
00:54:19,966 --> 00:54:21,676
Patricia… Patricia, leave!

835
00:54:22,134 --> 00:54:23,719
Go! Go. Leave.

836
00:54:23,803 --> 00:54:25,763
-Ricardo, go with Patricia.
-Let's go.

837
00:54:25,846 --> 00:54:26,973
I'm okay.

838
00:54:27,348 --> 00:54:28,432
Go. Go!

839
00:54:36,691 --> 00:54:37,733
Wait.

840
00:54:41,946 --> 00:54:42,989
No.

841
00:54:44,115 --> 00:54:45,241
Patricia…

842
00:54:50,997 --> 00:54:52,039
Patricia…

843
00:54:52,456 --> 00:54:54,458
Yes, I'm the girl in the video.

844
00:54:58,295 --> 00:55:00,715
But that's not the whole truth.

845
00:55:03,175 --> 00:55:04,593
What really happened…

846
00:55:05,344 --> 00:55:07,471
was my director fooled me.

847
00:55:09,849 --> 00:55:11,684
He told me…

848
00:55:12,476 --> 00:55:15,980
that it was for an indie film,
but that was a lie.

849
00:55:17,898 --> 00:55:19,984
They took advantage of me.

850
00:55:20,860 --> 00:55:22,737
But nothing bad happened.

851
00:55:24,113 --> 00:55:27,575
I was saved by Enzo and Ms. D.

852
00:55:30,036 --> 00:55:32,371
I have nothing to be ashamed of.

853
00:55:33,706 --> 00:55:35,082
I fought back,

854
00:55:37,460 --> 00:55:40,463
unlike what the video
tried to make it seem.

855
00:55:44,425 --> 00:55:48,012
The victim should not
suffer embarrassment!

856
00:55:50,264 --> 00:55:51,474
Who should be embarrassed are the creator…

857
00:55:52,683 --> 00:55:58,272
and the person
who showed it to the public.

858
00:56:00,608 --> 00:56:02,401
I will not let myself…

859
00:56:02,735 --> 00:56:05,279
be ruined by this video!

860
00:56:07,740 --> 00:56:12,453
Because I will never accept

861
00:56:12,536 --> 00:56:14,663
and I will never let myself…

862
00:56:15,915 --> 00:56:18,709
be a mere victim in your eyes!

863
00:56:24,632 --> 00:56:25,633
Patricia.

864
00:56:25,716 --> 00:56:26,801
Let's go.

865
00:57:17,101 --> 00:57:18,227
Patricia?

866
00:57:24,733 --> 00:57:26,694
I'm not going back there.

867
00:57:28,612 --> 00:57:29,905
Hey, hey…

868
00:57:30,573 --> 00:57:31,782
It's okay.

869
00:57:31,866 --> 00:57:33,033
Patricia…

870
00:57:34,493 --> 00:57:35,619
Hey…

871
00:57:36,579 --> 00:57:37,663
Hey…

872
00:57:38,289 --> 00:57:41,876
Look, I'm not letting you
go back there, okay?

873
00:57:43,502 --> 00:57:45,671
Yes. Okay? I'm here.

874
00:57:46,797 --> 00:57:49,300
Okay? It's okay.

875
00:57:51,010 --> 00:57:52,511
It's okay. It's okay.

876
00:57:55,181 --> 00:57:56,515
It's okay, it's okay.

877
00:57:58,601 --> 00:57:59,727
I'm here.

878
00:58:15,576 --> 00:58:17,661
Breathe, breathe.

879
00:58:18,495 --> 00:58:19,788
It's okay.

880
00:58:21,415 --> 00:58:22,958
It's okay, Patricia.

881
00:58:24,835 --> 00:58:26,212
It's okay.

882
00:58:26,295 --> 00:58:27,463
Breathe.

883
00:58:27,546 --> 00:58:28,589
It's okay.

884
00:58:41,060 --> 00:58:42,269
Are you really that desperate for fame

885
00:58:42,353 --> 00:58:43,604
-that you'd do that?
-Hey.

886
00:58:43,687 --> 00:58:44,563
She's a victim.

887
00:58:44,647 --> 00:58:46,774
Why didn't you tell Martin about this?

888
00:58:46,857 --> 00:58:48,984
You can't protect our daughter.

889
00:58:49,068 --> 00:58:51,487
Her life's been a mess since she got here!

890
00:58:51,570 --> 00:58:52,821
Dad, that's enough.

891
00:58:52,905 --> 00:58:54,698
This is an attack against me.

892
00:58:54,782 --> 00:58:57,576
Why would they drag my daughter into this?

893
00:58:57,660 --> 00:58:59,954
I hope Aunt Diana never let you in here.

894
00:59:00,037 --> 00:59:02,748
You will never amount to anything.

895
00:59:02,831 --> 00:59:05,793
Between the two of us, I am more worthy.

896
00:59:05,876 --> 00:59:07,336
That's the flash drive I brought in, sir.

897
00:59:07,628 --> 00:59:09,380
Then, where did that video come from?

898
00:59:09,463 --> 00:59:10,881
I don't want to go to jail, Daddy!

899
00:59:11,298 --> 00:59:13,384
-No…
-You won't go to jail.

900
00:59:13,467 --> 00:59:14,843
They won't be able to prove it.

901
00:59:14,927 --> 00:59:17,513
I was paid to do it.
But my conscience is eating away at me.

902
00:59:17,596 --> 00:59:20,099
Who told you to do it? Tell me!

903
00:59:20,474 --> 00:59:21,392
It's him.

904
00:59:22,559 --> 00:59:26,146
I'm giving you a chance
to take control of your life.

905
00:59:26,230 --> 00:59:28,065
It's so easy for you to give up on me.

906
00:59:28,148 --> 00:59:30,359
Well, you never defended me, anyway.

907
00:59:30,442 --> 00:59:32,778
A lot of people are waiting
for my downfall.

908
00:59:32,861 --> 00:59:34,446
And they'd drag you down with me.

909
00:59:34,530 --> 00:59:36,365
I'm protecting you.
